# agentguard scanning itself.
#
# This repository ships attack samples on purpose. They are inert data — test
# fixtures, rule patterns and documentation quotes — not instructions addressed
# to a reader. Without these exclusions agentguard reports its own corpus as
# hostile, which would make the self-scan in CI meaningless.
#
# This is a declared skip, not a hidden one: CI prints how many files were
# skipped, and the reason is written down here.
#
# Note the shape of the problem. A tool that detects injection payloads has to
# contain injection payloads: in its rules, in its tests, and in its docs. Every
# one of those self-matches. There is no clever fix — only a declared boundary.

# Test corpus and the assertions that exercise the rules against it.
tests/

# Documents that quote payloads verbatim in order to explain the attack.
FINDINGS.md
README.md

# The rule set itself. Each rule's "regex" field contains the literal strings
# the rule looks for, so rules.json trivially matches its own patterns.
rules.json
